  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nBulk of precipitation should generally dissipate tonight, but \nan additional shortwave late tonight could keep a few light \nshowers going, possibly an isolated storm but generally \ninstability will be waning by then. \n\nSecondary shortwave exits by early Friday morning, with rebounding \nheights taking hold across the area, and a mainly dry, but continued \nwarm Friday on tap. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nAnother round of strong to severe storms is expected \nSaturday afternoon and evening, as a strong cold front moves into \nthe area. Better instability, and dynamics/deep layer shear, look to \nbe across SE Ohio and the Mid Ohio Valley region during the period, \nand SPC has placed this area in a slight risk. Damaging winds look \nto be the primary hazard during this time. The good news with this \nsystem, is much of the area should get a wetting rain out of it, at \nleast temporarily dampening fire concerns. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 3...\n\nCold front will exit to the east late Saturday night \ninto early Sunday, with drier conditions taking hold as high \npressure builds into the area. Frost and freeze conditions will be \npossible early next week, along with very low afternoon relative \nhumidity.",
